      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "CREDIBILITY (3) is knocking on the door, having fought hard when beaten a long neck at Grafton after also closing in to second at Muswellbrook despite being held up in the straight. Has the right profile to break through now and should appreciate the rise in trip. DUN DARTE CHEAP (4) has mixed his form this time in but his good performances are up to this on the quick back-up. Has raced best when ridden positive, so wouldn't be surprised to see them push forward from the wide draw. TISANI JAMES (9) has been around the mark without placing and he was okay on the course proper last time when finishing fourth after leading them up. The shorter trip looks more suitable. BOSCATINE (1) returns freshened after a plain Gold Coast run, his fifth here two back is a better guide to his chances. Keeps the claim and is in the mix.",
